# llama-swap binary plus the pinned copies kept for rollback (v265 .. v271):
# ~46 MB each, per-release downloads or build output. run-llama-swap.sh takes
# LLAMA_SWAP=/path/to/llama-swap when it lives elsewhere.
/llama-swap
/llama-swap.v*

# release archives unpacked into the copies above
/*.tar.gz

# upstream llama-swap changelog package (Go source + the v*.md notes it embeds):
# vendored, and nothing here builds it - no go.mod, no importer
/changelog/

# the tarball's own upstream docs: extracted beside the binary, nothing of ours.
# LICENSE.md is llama-swap's own MIT text and carries Benson Wong's copyright, so
# it belongs upstream: this repo publishes its config and launchers, not a
# license that could be read as claiming someone else's work as ours.
/README.md
/CHANGELOG.md
/LICENSE.md

# Loom's gufo, built by ./nix-loom-build.sh and pointed at the resulting
# /nix/store path by ./nix-loom-gufo.sh. Absolute symlinks into a store path that
# only exists on this box, so a clone gets two dead links and no hint. Build them
# yourself; loom/README.md walks through it.
/loom/gufo
/loom/gufo-server

# runtime droppings
*.log
*.pid
*.sock
